WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.638 --> 00:00:19.801
After Inspector Lestrade departed, Sherlock Holmes made his preparations for the day.

2
00:00:20.641 --> 00:00:23.362
He was acting like a man who had a pleasant task ahead of him.

3
00:00:23.382 --> 00:00:28.745
"My first move, Watson," he said as he bustled into his coat, "must be in the direction of

4
00:00:28.785 --> 00:00:30.506
McFarlane's parents in Blackheath."

5
00:00:30.526 --> 00:00:33.288
"Why not Norwood, the scene of the crime?"

6
00:00:33.672 --> 00:00:34.092
I asked.

7
00:00:34.112 --> 00:00:39.995
"Because in this case we have one strange incident coming right after another strange incident," said Holmes.

8
00:00:40.015 --> 00:00:43.676
"The police are concentrating on the second incident—the murder.

9
00:00:44.497 --> 00:00:48.639
But it's obvious to me that the way to approach this case is to concentrate on the first

10
00:00:48.699 --> 00:00:54.141
incident—the unusual will, which Oldacre made so suddenly and with such an unexpected heir."

11
00:00:54.161 --> 00:00:56.042
"Would you like me to come along?"

12
00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:56.902
I asked him.

13
00:00:56.922 --> 00:01:00.664
"No." A smile flickered across his face.

14
00:01:01.724 --> 00:01:04.806
"If there were a chance of danger, I wouldn't dream of leaving you behind.

15
00:01:05.647 --> 00:01:06.988
But I don't think you can help me here.

16
00:01:07.928 --> 00:01:11.130
I trust that by the time I see you this evening, I will have been able to help

17
00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.431
this unfortunate young man."

18
00:01:13.372 --> 00:01:15.733
It was late when the detective returned to our lodgings.

19
00:01:16.654 --> 00:01:20.536
With a glance at his tired and anxious face, I could see that his high hopes for the

20
00:01:20.576 --> 00:01:21.837
day had not been fulfilled.

21
00:01:22.678 --> 00:01:26.240
For an hour he played his violin, trying to soothe his own ruffled spirits.

22
00:01:27.236 --> 00:01:31.578
At last he flung down the instrument and plunged into a detailed account of his misadventures.

23
00:01:31.598 --> 00:01:35.039
"It's all going wrong, Watson, as wrong as it can go.

24
00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:39.501
For once in my life, I believe Lestrade is on the right track and we are on the

25
00:01:39.521 --> 00:01:39.982
wrong one.

26
00:01:40.862 --> 00:01:44.023
All my instincts are on one side, and all the facts are on the other."

27
00:01:44.864 --> 00:01:46.925
"Did you go to Blackheath to see McFarlane's parents?"

28
00:01:47.325 --> 00:01:47.745
I asked.

29
00:01:49.366 --> 00:01:54.648
"Yes, and I learned very quickly that the late, lamented Oldacre was quite a scoundrel," replied Holmes.

30
00:01:55.616 --> 00:01:59.057
When Holmes arrived, McFarlane's father was out in search of his son.

31
00:01:59.957 --> 00:02:03.098
McFarlane's mother would not admit even the possibility of her son's guilt.

32
00:02:04.018 --> 00:02:06.519
But she expressed no regret over Oldacre's fate.

33
00:02:07.539 --> 00:02:12.101
On the contrary, she spoke of him with such bitterness that Holmes felt she could have predisposed her

34
00:02:12.121 --> 00:02:13.581
son to hate and kill the builder.

35
00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:16.782
"I knew Oldacre when he was a young man," Mrs.

36
00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:17.802
McFarlane told Holmes.

37
00:02:17.822 --> 00:02:22.743
"In fact, I was engaged to him when I heard a shocking story of how he had turned

38
00:02:22.783 --> 00:02:26.449
a cat loose in an aviary, where it could catch and kill the birds.

39
00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:31.112
I was so horrified at his brutal cruelty that I would have nothing more to do with him.

40
00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:35.135
Thank heaven, I had the sense to marry a better, if poorer, man."

41
00:02:36.816 --> 00:02:42.200
She rummaged in a bureau and soon produced a woman's photograph, horribly defaced and mutilated with a knife.

42
00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:45.642
"This is my own photograph," she said to Holmes.

43
00:02:45.662 --> 00:02:49.725
"On my wedding day Oldacre sent it to me like this with his curse."

44
00:02:49.745 --> 00:02:55.260
"Well, at least he has forgiven you now," said Holmes, "since he has left all his property to

45
00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:55.821
your son."

46
00:02:55.841 --> 00:03:00.642
"Neither my son nor I want anything from Jonas Oldacre, dead or alive!"

47
00:03:01.022 --> 00:03:01.562
she cried.

48
00:03:02.442 --> 00:03:03.763
Holmes could get nothing from Mrs.

49
00:03:03.803 --> 00:03:07.984
McFarlane that would help her son's case, so he moved on to Oldacre's house in Norwood.

50
00:03:08.824 --> 00:03:11.545
Lestrade had left, but several of his policemen were still there.

51
00:03:12.385 --> 00:03:16.086
They had just found something of great interest while raking through the ashes of the fire.

52
00:03:16.966 --> 00:03:20.667
Besides the charred remains, they had discovered several discolored metal disks.

53
00:03:21.688 --> 00:03:25.381
Holmes examined them with care, and there was no doubt that they were trouser buttons.

54
00:03:27.141 --> 00:03:29.502
One of them was even marked with the name of Oldacre's tailor.

55
00:03:29.522 --> 00:03:34.903
"I then went over the lawn very carefully for any footprints or signs of the crime," Holmes said

56
00:03:34.943 --> 00:03:35.183
to me.

57
00:03:35.203 --> 00:03:38.524
"But the recent drought had made the ground as hard as rock.

58
00:03:39.544 --> 00:03:43.726
Nothing was to be seen except that some body or bundle had been dragged to the lumber yard."

59
00:03:44.686 --> 00:03:47.927
Next Holmes went to Oldacre's bedroom, where he examined the bloodstains.

60
00:03:48.867 --> 00:03:52.508
The walking stick had been removed, but our client had already admitted it was his.

61
00:03:53.556 --> 00:03:56.758
Holmes could see both Oldacre's and McFarlane's footprints on the carpet.

62
00:03:57.598 --> 00:04:02.301
There was no sign that anyone else had been present, which did not help McFarlane's case either.

63
00:04:02.321 --> 00:04:05.042
"Couldn't you find anything to benefit our client?"

64
00:04:05.383 --> 00:04:06.023
I asked Holmes.

65
00:04:06.043 --> 00:04:09.465
"There was only one little gleam of hope," said Holmes.

66
00:04:09.485 --> 00:04:13.527
"I examined the contents of the safe, which had been left on the table.

67
00:04:15.148 --> 00:04:17.849
As far as I could tell, the papers were not of any great value.

68
00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:22.132
Some of them referred to valuable deeds, but I could not find these deeds.

69
00:04:23.084 --> 00:04:29.187
That may work in McFarlane's favor because—to use Lestrade's argument—the heir wouldn't need to steal documents he was

70
00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:30.088
going to inherit."

71
00:04:31.088 --> 00:04:34.310
Before he left, Holmes decided to try his luck with the housekeeper, Mrs.

72
00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:38.512
Lexington. "She could tell us something if she wanted to," Holmes said to me.

73
00:04:38.532 --> 00:04:41.814
"But she refused to say anything more than necessary."

74
00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.816
Yes, she had let McFarlane in the night before.

75
00:04:45.716 --> 00:04:47.397
She had gone to bed at half past ten.

76
00:04:48.358 --> 00:04:51.960
Her room was at the other end of the house, so she heard nothing of what passed between

77
00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:52.440
the two men.

78
00:04:53.428 --> 00:04:55.170
She had been awakened by the alarm of fire.

79
00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.312
Her poor, dear master had certainly been murdered.

80
00:04:59.273 --> 00:05:02.776
She had seen the buttons and was sure that they belonged to the clothes that he had worn

81
00:05:02.816 --> 00:05:03.316
last night.

82
00:05:04.277 --> 00:05:06.699
She knew nothing of the papers nor of Mr.

83
00:05:06.799 --> 00:05:08.100
Oldacre's private affairs.

84
00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:13.704
"So, my dear Watson, there's my report of failure," Holmes said.

85
00:05:13.724 --> 00:05:18.108
"And yet—and yet—" He clenched his thin hands.

86
00:05:18.128 --> 00:05:20.690
"I know something is wrong.

87
00:05:21.631 --> 00:05:22.732
I feel it in my bones.

88
00:05:23.696 --> 00:05:26.878
There is a detail that has not come out, and that housekeeper knows it.

89
00:05:27.759 --> 00:05:32.142
There was a sort of sulky defiance in her eyes, which only goes with a guilty conscience.

90
00:05:33.282 --> 00:05:35.444
Oh, there's no use talking about this anymore!"

91
00:05:36.384 --> 00:05:37.425
"Surely you are not giving up?"

92
00:05:37.825 --> 00:05:38.245
I asked.

93
00:05:39.306 --> 00:05:42.928
"No, but unless we can establish an alternative theory, McFarlane is lost."

94
00:05:43.969 --> 00:05:44.750
Holmes paused.

95
00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:48.312
"There was one unusual thing among those papers.

96
00:05:49.404 --> 00:05:54.448
Oldacre's bankbook showed that he didn't have much money, a surprising fact given that he was supposed to

97
00:05:54.489 --> 00:05:55.409
be a wealthy man.

98
00:05:56.290 --> 00:06:01.194
His low bank balance was principally due to large checks that were written in the last year to

99
00:06:01.254 --> 00:06:01.675
a Mr.

100
00:06:01.735 --> 00:06:05.138
Cornelius." "I wonder who this Mr.

101
00:06:05.178 --> 00:06:06.879
Cornelius is," I said.

102
00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:12.204
"Yes, I will have to investigate the gentleman who cashed those checks," said Holmes.

103
00:06:12.224 --> 00:06:17.168
"But I still fear, Watson, that our case will end with Lestrade hanging our client."

104
00:06:18.016 --> 00:06:21.997
I don't know if Holmes managed to sleep that night, but when I came down to breakfast, I

105
00:06:22.057 --> 00:06:23.738
found him looking pale and harassed.

106
00:06:24.658 --> 00:06:28.339
The carpet around his chair was littered with the early editions of the morning papers.

107
00:06:29.359 --> 00:06:30.960
An open telegram lay on the table.

108
00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.300
"What do you think of this, Watson?"

109
00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.721
He tossed the telegram over to me.

110
00:06:36.661 --> 00:06:41.502
It was from Norwood and ran as follows: Important fresh evidence has been discovered.

111
00:06:42.323 --> 00:06:44.323
McFarlane's guilt definitely established.

112
00:06:45.283 --> 00:06:46.904
Advise you to abandon the case.

113
00:06:47.328 --> 00:06:47.870
Lestrade
